1
00:01:20,126 --> 00:01:21,126
'2026'

2
00:01:21,246 --> 00:01:22,526
'2026
Election day'

3
00:01:22,845 --> 00:01:25,644
'At a time when elections are
in full swing across Tamil Nadu'

4
00:01:25,645 --> 00:01:28,605
'Due to caste issues
residents of Pappampatti village'

5
00:01:28,606 --> 00:01:30,725
'Boycotted the election for the 3rd time'

6
00:01:31,005 --> 00:01:32,725
[siren wailing]

7
00:01:36,725 --> 00:01:38,484
Get ready, all of you
Come and vote

8
00:01:38,485 --> 00:01:41,285
The right to vote is the civic duty
of every Indian citizen to uphold

9
00:01:41,406 --> 00:01:43,284
Sir, we are ready to vote

10
00:01:43,285 --> 00:01:46,085
But knowing none of us
will vote for their Party

11
00:01:46,285 --> 00:01:48,405
They have denied us
the right to vote freely, sir

12
00:01:48,406 --> 00:01:50,326
See the fate of those
who defied them and voted

13
00:01:50,845 --> 00:01:52,126
[dramatic music]

14
00:01:55,766 --> 00:01:59,765
We can't vote one day and then
live in fear the whole year through, sir

15
00:01:59,766 --> 00:02:01,805
They will hit us
even if we go to school, sir

16
00:02:01,806 --> 00:02:03,326
We will be so terrified

17
00:02:07,085 --> 00:02:09,646
My dear child, whenever I feel scared

18
00:02:09,926 --> 00:02:12,366
I will think of one man's story

19
00:02:12,725 --> 00:02:15,285
Immediately my fear will vanish
and my heart will brim with courage

20
00:02:15,845 --> 00:02:17,806
Shall I narrate that story of courage?

21
00:02:19,165 --> 00:02:21,045
That Mr Courage is

22
00:02:21,565 --> 00:02:22,564
'Thalapathy'

23
00:02:22,565 --> 00:02:23,806
'VI'

24
00:02:24,246 --> 00:02:25,246
[upbeat music]

25
00:02:26,005 --> 00:02:27,126
'J'

26
00:02:29,086 --> 00:02:30,246
'AY'

27
00:02:31,966 --> 00:02:32,965
Honorable

28
00:02:32,966 --> 00:02:34,325
Tamil Nadu
Chief Minister

29
00:02:34,765 --> 00:02:37,164
Honorable Chief Minister of Tamil Nadu
C Joseph Vijay

30
00:02:37,165 --> 00:02:39,646
Honorable Chief Minister of Tamil Nadu
Thalapathy C Joseph Vijay

31
00:02:42,806 --> 00:02:44,845
'Madurai
2013'

32
00:02:50,445 --> 00:02:51,765
[gate opens]

33
00:02:53,445 --> 00:02:54,806
[suspenseful music]

34
00:02:57,725 --> 00:02:59,406
[mobile ringing]

35
00:03:00,045 --> 00:03:01,086
Tell me, Narayanan

36
00:03:01,246 --> 00:03:03,724
Sir, 20 rowdies have surrendered here

37
00:03:03,725 --> 00:03:06,686
Shall I proceed with the admission
or wait until you get here?

38
00:03:06,806 --> 00:03:08,965
I am shifting my quarters
I won't be coming right now

39
00:03:08,966 --> 00:03:10,044
Complete the formalities

40
00:03:10,045 --> 00:03:11,725
- 'Take them to Admission Block'
- Okay, sir

41
00:03:12,285 --> 00:03:13,605
[suspenseful music intensifies]

42
00:03:17,005 --> 00:03:18,246
[phone ringing]

43
00:03:19,126 --> 00:03:21,125
Is there any important prisoner
in Admission Block?

44
00:03:21,126 --> 00:03:22,165
Yes, sir

45
00:03:22,445 --> 00:03:24,045
'Loganathan
Business man'

46
00:03:24,206 --> 00:03:25,806
'Opposition's key funder'

47
00:03:26,165 --> 00:03:27,926
'He has been locked up
under a put-up case'

48
00:03:28,406 --> 00:03:29,565
STOP THEM!

49
00:03:30,045 --> 00:03:31,045
[alarm blaring]

50
00:03:32,646 --> 00:03:33,966
[thrilling music]

51
00:03:39,045 --> 00:03:40,246
[gates closing]

52
00:03:46,765 --> 00:03:48,604
I am on the way
What's the situation?

53
00:03:48,605 --> 00:03:49,645
Sir

54
00:03:49,646 --> 00:03:50,725
Take your time

55
00:03:50,845 --> 00:03:52,325
They have gone into C Block

56
00:03:52,445 --> 00:03:53,406
So...?

57
00:03:54,366 --> 00:03:56,445
Thalapathy is there, sir

58
00:03:56,646 --> 00:03:58,086
[continuous commotion]

59
00:03:58,445 --> 00:04:00,325
'Indian Democracy'

60
00:04:00,445 --> 00:04:01,445
[thuds]

61
00:04:02,926 --> 00:04:05,565
[grandiose music]

62
00:04:13,165 --> 00:04:15,646
[grandiose music continues]

63
00:04:27,005 --> 00:04:28,205
[man screaming]

64
00:04:31,366 --> 00:04:32,325
[short whistle]

65
00:04:35,286 --> 00:04:36,366
Hey! Kill him

66
00:04:36,645 --> 00:04:37,846
[snaps finger]

67
00:04:38,005 --> 00:04:39,205
'Bro, 1 minute'

68
00:04:40,126 --> 00:04:41,925
'When you were
playing hide & seek'

69
00:04:41,926 --> 00:04:44,404
'You knocked down this grandpa
and disturbed his sleep'

70
00:04:44,405 --> 00:04:46,004
'Make sure our grandpa gets his due rest'

71
00:04:46,005 --> 00:04:47,324
'Then continue your game'

72
00:04:47,325 --> 00:04:48,365
Game, huh?

73
00:04:48,366 --> 00:04:50,445
Hey! We plan to kill now
Turn back and go

74
00:04:55,846 --> 00:04:57,445
This seems to be a new struggle

75
00:04:57,565 --> 00:04:59,806
First, make him rest in peace, da

76
00:05:01,205 --> 00:05:02,205
[suspenseful music]

77
00:05:07,126 --> 00:05:08,046
[sharp thuds]

78
00:05:09,885 --> 00:05:11,246
[thuds and thwacks]

79
00:05:15,205 --> 00:05:17,565
[enthralling music]

80
00:05:18,525 --> 00:05:20,405
[fire sparkling]

81
00:05:24,046 --> 00:05:26,405
[theme song plays]

82
00:05:42,846 --> 00:05:46,525
'JANA NAYAGAN'

83
00:05:46,645 --> 00:05:50,286
'PEOPLE'S LEADER'

84
00:05:51,366 --> 00:05:53,366
[sharp music]

85
00:06:02,965 --> 00:06:05,126
[sharp music continues]

86
00:06:11,686 --> 00:06:13,686
If you didn't hear me clearly
I'll repeat it for your ears

87
00:06:14,366 --> 00:06:16,286
Grandpa has to sleep

88
00:06:20,726 --> 00:06:23,286
Lord and master!
I am your slave

89
00:06:23,806 --> 00:06:25,806
First, grandpa has to rest in ease

90
00:06:25,926 --> 00:06:28,806
Only then, Logan Baba will rest in peace!

91
00:06:29,445 --> 00:06:30,445
Okay?

92
00:06:30,806 --> 00:06:31,846
Go back, da

93
00:06:32,126 --> 00:06:33,885
Grandpa, lie on a human water bed

94
00:06:34,126 --> 00:06:36,365
How does it feel?
Cool and comfy, uh?

95
00:06:36,366 --> 00:06:37,644
Sleep, my child

96
00:06:37,645 --> 00:06:40,525
If you sing me a lullaby
I'll happily slip into dream world

97
00:06:40,806 --> 00:06:42,085
What, thatha?

98
00:06:42,885 --> 00:06:45,726
- You seem to be in a jolly mood!
- [chuckles]

99
00:06:45,885 --> 00:06:47,405
What are you gaping at me for?

100
00:06:48,606 --> 00:06:49,645
Sing, I say

101
00:06:50,005 --> 00:06:52,925
"Grandpa, just a pinch I need
Give me your snuff powder, I plead"

102
00:06:52,926 --> 00:06:56,405
"Grandson, pass my stick,
I'll whack you double quick"

103
00:06:57,046 --> 00:06:59,645
"Grandpa, just a pinch I need
Give me your snuff powder, I plead"

104
00:07:00,126 --> 00:07:03,366
"Grandson, pass my stick,
I'll whack you double quick"

105
00:07:03,486 --> 00:07:07,325
"When grandpa grabbed his stick to hit
the snuff powder flew into thin air, swift"

106
00:07:07,445 --> 00:07:09,365
"Grampsssss"

107
00:07:09,366 --> 00:07:10,445
Hey!

108
00:07:11,005 --> 00:07:13,726
I asked you to sing for thatha to sleep
you're making him dance and leap!

109
00:07:13,885 --> 00:07:14,926
HEY!

110
00:07:15,085 --> 00:07:16,445
- Hey... hey!
- Shhhhh!

111
00:07:16,965 --> 00:07:18,405
What? Going overboard?

112
00:07:18,565 --> 00:07:20,205
My bro came here on a killing mission

113
00:07:20,325 --> 00:07:21,926
You want him to preach now!

114
00:07:22,246 --> 00:07:24,246
[mocks]

115
00:07:25,046 --> 00:07:26,046
[smacks]

116
00:07:26,645 --> 00:07:27,806
- [sharp kicks]
- 'Aiyaiyo!'

117
00:07:28,926 --> 00:07:30,846
[song from 'Kadhalukku Mariyadhai' plays]

118
00:07:31,085 --> 00:07:33,205
Bingo! He'll sleep like a baby now

119
00:07:33,686 --> 00:07:36,885
"Will she sing me a lullaby?"

120
00:07:37,445 --> 00:07:40,686
"Rest my head in her bosom like a baby?"

121
00:07:41,405 --> 00:07:44,926
"Will she move with flowing grace
as a golden chariot to this place?"

122
00:07:45,445 --> 00:07:49,085
"Or disappoint my heart
by drifting apart?"

123
00:07:49,246 --> 00:07:50,405
Hey wait... wait

124
00:07:50,726 --> 00:07:54,324
"Be patient, sing no more
I can hear him snore"

125
00:07:54,325 --> 00:07:55,686
'He is fast asleep'

126
00:07:57,005 --> 00:07:58,645
[loud snore]

127
00:08:02,166 --> 00:08:04,046
- [thwacks]
- [man screams softly]

128
00:08:09,286 --> 00:08:10,525
[blows out]

129
00:08:12,645 --> 00:08:16,205
"The entire town is in slumber deep"

130
00:08:16,486 --> 00:08:20,246
"Even the cool breeze has started to sweep'

131
00:08:20,405 --> 00:08:24,126
"But sleep eludes this blessed grandfather"

132
00:08:24,366 --> 00:08:28,444
"Wonder why, I'm clueless, brother"

133
00:08:28,445 --> 00:08:31,365
Bro! I told you to close his chapter
You are partying, singing together?

134
00:08:31,366 --> 00:08:32,804
- Sssshhh!
- HUH?

135
00:08:32,805 --> 00:08:33,804
Hey!
[quiet whisper]

136
00:08:33,805 --> 00:08:35,284
Grandpa is sleeping
Keep quiet

137
00:08:35,285 --> 00:08:37,726
What is this, bro?
You keep saying 'grandpa... sleep'?

138
00:08:38,645 --> 00:08:40,645
- Move aside, bro
- [sharp kicks]

139
00:08:45,805 --> 00:08:48,764
"Death's quiet whisper
drifted into my ear"

140
00:08:48,765 --> 00:08:52,405
"It appeared here as an image
of a king with confidence and courage"

141
00:08:53,165 --> 00:08:54,486
[winces]

142
00:08:55,366 --> 00:08:57,925
[gripping energetic music]

143
00:09:08,405 --> 00:09:09,925
[sharp thwack]

144
00:09:11,765 --> 00:09:13,005
[loud thud]

145
00:09:13,525 --> 00:09:16,045
Listen to the advice of youngsters, da

146
00:09:19,446 --> 00:09:22,405
[gripping energetic music continues]

147
00:09:27,726 --> 00:09:29,165
Hai!

148
00:09:30,726 --> 00:09:33,326
[action ensues]

149
00:09:40,326 --> 00:09:43,446
[gripping energetic music continues]

150
00:09:48,165 --> 00:09:49,365
Telling us to make him sleep

151
00:09:49,366 --> 00:09:51,206
You'll end up making us rest in peace!?

152
00:09:51,486 --> 00:09:52,804
'Please open the door'

153
00:09:52,805 --> 00:09:53,966
He is very dangerous

154
00:09:54,206 --> 00:09:55,405
Arrest them

155
00:09:55,966 --> 00:09:57,366
This is the best time to act

156
00:09:57,645 --> 00:09:59,566
With issues overlapping
we can finish him off

157
00:10:00,446 --> 00:10:02,326
- [crowd cheering]
- [ominous music]

158
00:10:05,446 --> 00:10:06,765
Problem is spiraling

159
00:10:06,925 --> 00:10:08,005
Open the gate

160
00:10:08,326 --> 00:10:09,325
Sir

161
00:10:09,326 --> 00:10:10,326
Till now

162
00:10:10,486 --> 00:10:12,405
They have tried to kill him 20 times

163
00:10:12,685 --> 00:10:14,885
But even to edge close to him

164
00:10:15,206 --> 00:10:17,005
They have to go past
Vanamaran and Nelamaran

165
00:10:17,805 --> 00:10:20,086
Escape from the threatening gaze
of Kadamban and Kangeyam

166
00:10:21,285 --> 00:10:23,966
Retaliate to the power
of Murugan and Velan

167
00:10:25,966 --> 00:10:27,164
'I got a gang'

168
00:10:27,165 --> 00:10:29,086
'We run the space
Bang bang'

169
00:10:31,005 --> 00:10:32,005
'Say, what?'

170
00:10:32,925 --> 00:10:34,165
'I got a gang'

171
00:10:34,326 --> 00:10:36,206
'We run the space
Bang bang'

172
00:10:37,086 --> 00:10:39,206
[upbeat music]

173
00:10:44,326 --> 00:10:46,366
The day he was arrested
and brought here

174
00:10:46,606 --> 00:10:48,005
Not only inside the jail, sir

175
00:10:48,126 --> 00:10:50,645
Even outside, they settled
as an army to protect him

176
00:10:50,805 --> 00:10:52,726
Thalapathy is not
under our protection, sir

177
00:10:53,246 --> 00:10:55,566
Just the opposite, we are
under Thalapathy's protection

178
00:10:56,966 --> 00:10:58,245
'I got a gang'

179
00:10:58,246 --> 00:10:59,726
'We run the space
Bang bang'

180
00:11:00,846 --> 00:11:01,925
Sir... sir

181
00:11:03,525 --> 00:11:06,366
You staked your life to save mine

182
00:11:06,925 --> 00:11:07,966
Thank you, sir

183
00:11:08,246 --> 00:11:11,126
I won't sit quiet watching
any crime happening around me

184
00:11:12,765 --> 00:11:13,805
I will show up

185
00:11:14,206 --> 00:11:16,206
Sir... er, may I know your name?

186
00:11:17,005 --> 00:11:18,885
[heroic music]

187
00:11:24,645 --> 00:11:25,966
- Narayanan
- 'Sir?'

188
00:11:26,086 --> 00:11:27,525
I want to see his files

189
00:11:28,685 --> 00:11:31,126
[pulsating music]

190
00:11:32,765 --> 00:11:34,966
[dusting off]

191
00:11:38,446 --> 00:11:40,366
You hit a battalion of prisoners

192
00:11:40,606 --> 00:11:42,005
Are you Superman?

193
00:11:43,206 --> 00:11:45,366
[pulsating music continues]

194
00:11:46,885 --> 00:11:49,966
[upbeat music]

195
00:11:53,525 --> 00:11:55,566
I am an ordinary man, baby

196
00:11:55,726 --> 00:11:58,765
But I have heard people say
whatever I do is sooper!

197
00:11:58,885 --> 00:12:00,726
Then you are proper 'Superman' in my eyes

198
00:12:01,966 --> 00:12:02,965
Dishum!

199
00:12:02,966 --> 00:12:03,965
[playful giggle]

200
00:12:03,966 --> 00:12:05,446
Dishum-dishum

201
00:12:08,846 --> 00:12:11,245
Is his mother the reason
for him being here in jail?

202
00:12:11,246 --> 00:12:12,405
'Yes, sir'

203
00:12:14,285 --> 00:12:17,044
'Not enough if you keep lamenting
you want to see your son'

204
00:12:17,045 --> 00:12:19,126
Take your tablets regularly
if you want to see your son

205
00:12:19,246 --> 00:12:20,725
Atleast till your son comes

206
00:12:20,726 --> 00:12:22,765
You would've asked for bail
at least 50 times or so?

207
00:12:23,326 --> 00:12:24,606
Did they release him?

208
00:12:24,805 --> 00:12:26,086
She won't last long

209
00:12:26,366 --> 00:12:27,765
Doubtful if she will see her son

210
00:12:28,086 --> 00:12:31,165
No medicine is holding
my breath, doctor

211
00:12:32,206 --> 00:12:33,285
Love

212
00:12:34,285 --> 00:12:36,685
One last wish to see my son

213
00:12:38,966 --> 00:12:40,645
I will die only after I see him

214
00:12:41,126 --> 00:12:43,206
Sir, I'm begging you
I'll fall at your feet

215
00:12:44,126 --> 00:12:45,725
If you send our brother home

216
00:12:45,726 --> 00:12:49,405
Happily his mother will breathe her last
knowing she could see her son, sir

217
00:12:49,765 --> 00:12:54,245
Sir, they will wait with folded hands daily
when the previous jailer comes and leaves

218
00:12:54,246 --> 00:12:56,005
They didn't disperse
even when they were hit

219
00:12:56,285 --> 00:12:58,606
Direct orders from higher-ups
What can we do, sir?

220
00:12:59,326 --> 00:13:01,726
If I want to see my amma
you'll say she isn't here

221
00:13:01,966 --> 00:13:03,684
Superman's mother is alive

222
00:13:03,685 --> 00:13:05,165
Let's take him
to see his mother, pa

223
00:13:05,326 --> 00:13:06,326
[emotional music]

224
00:13:06,486 --> 00:13:07,566
Narayanan

225
00:13:07,885 --> 00:13:10,366
We are going to the forest
with Vetri tomorrow

226
00:13:11,366 --> 00:13:12,366
Okay?

227
00:13:12,925 --> 00:13:17,086
Son hearing his mother's cries of pain

228
00:13:17,246 --> 00:13:21,126
Crosses all barriers to see her again

229
00:13:21,246 --> 00:13:25,246
As the scars healed today
Wind too parted the way

230
00:13:25,366 --> 00:13:29,644
He is returning to bloom
in his mother's womb

231
00:13:29,645 --> 00:13:33,726
Back to the magic of my motherly lap

232
00:13:33,846 --> 00:13:37,446
Those childhood memories wrap
to replay in my mind's map

233
00:13:37,846 --> 00:13:41,645
A sky that vanished into the horizon

234
00:13:42,086 --> 00:13:45,566
Now returns as life's very reason

235
00:13:46,165 --> 00:13:50,126
My world spins again in a magical way

236
00:13:50,326 --> 00:13:53,366
Because you are my heart's mainstay

237
00:13:54,525 --> 00:13:58,326
My heart anew
brims with love so true

238
00:13:58,685 --> 00:14:01,285
Even if I die, I will live with you

239
00:14:03,805 --> 00:14:04,805
[sniffles]

240
00:14:23,405 --> 00:14:25,726
[emotional music continues]

241
00:14:36,405 --> 00:14:40,605
My poignant poetry
My tears of misery

242
00:14:40,606 --> 00:14:43,525
All reflect you in my story

243
00:14:44,805 --> 00:14:48,726
In my next birth, when I am a mother

244
00:14:48,885 --> 00:14:52,446
Even then you will be my child, no other

245
00:14:56,246 --> 00:14:58,765
My amma passed away
after seeing my face, sir

246
00:15:00,366 --> 00:15:03,285
You fulfilled my mother's last wish

247
00:15:04,765 --> 00:15:05,966
How will I thank-

248
00:15:08,486 --> 00:15:09,685
Thank you, sir

249
00:15:13,486 --> 00:15:16,925
Superman, don't feel bad
you lost your amma

250
00:15:17,086 --> 00:15:19,086
I'll be your amma hereafter

251
00:15:20,005 --> 00:15:22,045
[emotional music intensifies]

252
00:15:32,925 --> 00:15:34,206
Aah, open your mouth

253
00:15:40,165 --> 00:15:42,206
Your daughter looks smart
in army uniform, sir

254
00:15:42,685 --> 00:15:43,685
Yeah

255
00:15:43,846 --> 00:15:46,246
Actually my wife wanted
to join the military very badly

256
00:15:46,405 --> 00:15:50,404
Her parents didn't accept our love and
tried to get her married to someone else

257
00:15:50,405 --> 00:15:52,726
She cast her dream aside
and married me

258
00:15:52,846 --> 00:15:53,764
And

259
00:15:53,765 --> 00:15:56,285
She passed away
in last year's riot

260
00:15:59,405 --> 00:16:01,805
Every time she wore that uniform
and saw her reflection in the mirror

261
00:16:02,005 --> 00:16:04,446
I used to feel guilty
maybe I ruined her dreams

262
00:16:04,645 --> 00:16:05,846
After she was born

263
00:16:06,326 --> 00:16:09,285
She used to keep saying, 'I will
make your dream come true, ma'

264
